      "worked": "A line through $(3,-8)$ has equation\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny+8&=m(x-3)\\\\\ny&=mx-3m-8.\n\\end{align*}$$\nEquate the line and parabola:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2-1&=mx-3m-8\\\\\nx^2-mx+3m+7&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor tangency there is one intersection, so $\\Delta=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nm^2-4(3m+7)&=0\\\\\nm^2-12m-28&=0\\\\\n(m-14)(m+2)&=0\\\\\nm&=14\\text{ or }m=-2.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor $m=14$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny&=14x-3(14)-8\\\\\ny&=14x-50.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor $m=-2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny&=-2x-3(-2)-8\\\\\ny&=-2x-2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
